WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.281
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online B one, Book three.

2
00:00:05.581 --> 00:00:09.141
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.441 --> 00:00:15.205
Unit seventeen: Social Media Balance. Today you will give advice with It's important to.

4
00:00:15.505 --> 00:00:18.076
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:19.033 --> 00:00:22.115
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:22.950 --> 00:00:24.381
Social media.

7
00:00:25.383 --> 00:00:28.799
Social media means websites and apps for sharing online.

8
00:00:29.383 --> 00:00:31.824
I use social media to talk to friends.

9
00:00:32.417 --> 00:00:34.848
Your turn. Say: Social media.

10
00:00:37.700 --> 00:00:38.980
Social media.

11
00:00:39.717 --> 00:00:40.799
Screen time.

12
00:00:41.783 --> 00:00:44.468
Screen time means time spent looking at screens.

13
00:00:45.083 --> 00:00:47.524
My screen time was six hours yesterday!

14
00:00:48.117 --> 00:00:50.711
Your turn. Say: Screen time.

15
00:00:53.567 --> 00:00:55.113
Screen time.

16
00:00:55.850 --> 00:00:56.805
Balance.

17
00:00:57.817 --> 00:01:00.385
Balance means a healthy mix of different things.

18
00:01:00.983 --> 00:01:04.039
I try to keep a balance between online and offline.

19
00:01:04.650 --> 00:01:07.070
Your turn. Say: Balance.

20
00:01:09.933 --> 00:01:10.749
Balance.

21
00:01:11.483 --> 00:01:12.589
Disconnect.

22
00:01:13.583 --> 00:01:16.906
Disconnect means to stop using the internet for a while.

23
00:01:17.517 --> 00:01:19.412
I disconnect every Sunday.

24
00:01:20.017 --> 00:01:22.599
Your turn. Say: Disconnect.

25
00:01:25.433 --> 00:01:26.411
Disconnect.

26
00:01:27.150 --> 00:01:28.244
Real life.

27
00:01:29.250 --> 00:01:31.865
Real life means life outside the internet.

28
00:01:32.450 --> 00:01:34.659
Real-life friends are important.

29
00:01:35.250 --> 00:01:37.856
Your turn. Say: Real life.

30
00:01:40.700 --> 00:01:41.713
Real life.

31
00:01:42.450 --> 00:01:43.370
Addiction.

32
00:01:44.383 --> 00:01:47.370
Addiction means not being able to stop doing something.

33
00:01:47.983 --> 00:01:49.600
Phone addiction is common.

34
00:01:50.183 --> 00:01:52.789
Your turn. Say: Addiction.

35
00:01:55.633 --> 00:01:56.530
Addiction.

36
00:01:57.283 --> 00:01:58.029
Limit.

37
00:01:59.017 --> 00:02:00.981
Limit means the most that is allowed.

38
00:02:01.583 --> 00:02:03.653
Set a daily limit on your apps.

39
00:02:04.250 --> 00:02:06.763
Your turn. Say: Limit.

40
00:02:09.600 --> 00:02:10.427
Limit.

41
00:02:11.183 --> 00:02:12.161
Mindful.

42
00:02:13.150 --> 00:02:15.916
Mindful means careful and aware of what you are doing.

43
00:02:16.517 --> 00:02:18.702
Be mindful of how you feel online.

44
00:02:19.317 --> 00:02:21.574
Your turn. Say: Mindful.

45
00:02:24.433 --> 00:02:25.492
Mindful.

46
00:02:26.300 --> 00:02:29.823
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:30.683 --> 00:02:33.647
Visal, how much time do you spend on social media?

48
00:02:34.750 --> 00:02:37.472
Too much! Maybe five hours a day.

49
00:02:38.583 --> 00:02:40.780
It's important to limit screen time.

50
00:02:41.883 --> 00:02:44.594
I know. Sometimes I feel addicted.

51
00:02:45.683 --> 00:02:49.041
It's important to disconnect sometimes and enjoy real life.

52
00:02:50.150 --> 00:02:53.778
Good idea. I'll set a limit and be more mindful.

53
00:02:54.933 --> 00:02:56.422
Part three: grammar.

54
00:02:57.283 --> 00:03:00.374
Grammar focus: It's important to plus verb.

55
00:03:00.674 --> 00:03:01.977
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:02.683 --> 00:03:04.869
It's important to limit screen time.

57
00:03:05.783 --> 00:03:08.108
It's important to disconnect sometimes.

58
00:03:09.017 --> 00:03:11.283
It's important to be mindful online.

59
00:03:12.233 --> 00:03:16.090
Use 'It's important to' + base verb to give strong, general advice.

60
00:03:16.850 --> 00:03:20.245
Be careful! Don't say: It's important limit screen time.

61
00:03:22.200 --> 00:03:25.070
Say: It's important to limit screen time.

62
00:03:25.370 --> 00:03:27.718
Use 'to' + verb after 'It's important'.

63
00:03:28.533 --> 00:03:31.476
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

64
00:03:32.267 --> 00:03:34.011
Online and Offline.

65
00:03:34.311 --> 00:03:38.133
Finding a healthy balance with social media is not easy.

66
00:03:39.133 --> 00:03:41.702
It's important to be mindful of your screen time.

67
00:03:42.700 --> 00:03:46.244
It's important to disconnect sometimes and focus on real life.

68
00:03:47.233 --> 00:03:49.732
Setting a limit can help you avoid addiction.

69
00:03:50.733 --> 00:03:53.673
Real-life friends and activities make us happy.

70
00:03:54.767 --> 00:03:58.792
Part five: quiz. Three questions. Are you ready?

71
00:03:59.650 --> 00:04:01.626
It's important blank screen time.

72
00:04:01.926 --> 00:04:05.452
A, to limit. B, limit. C, limiting.

73
00:04:09.000 --> 00:04:10.779
The answer is A: to limit.

74
00:04:11.917 --> 00:04:14.938
To stop using the internet for a while is to blank.

75
00:04:15.238 --> 00:04:18.543
A, disconnect. B, limit. C, post.

76
00:04:22.100 --> 00:04:23.879
The answer is A: disconnect.

77
00:04:25.017 --> 00:04:27.701
Not being able to stop doing something is blank.

78
00:04:28.001 --> 00:04:31.585
A, addiction. B, balance. C, a limit.

79
00:04:35.133 --> 00:04:36.959
The answer is A: addiction.

80
00:04:38.167 --> 00:04:41.086
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

81
00:04:41.950 --> 00:04:45.366
How do you balance social media with real life activities?

82
00:04:54.150 --> 00:04:55.523
Now listen to Visal.

83
00:04:55.823 --> 00:05:03.955
I use social media for one hour after homework. It's important to disconnect, so I play football with my friends every evening.

84
00:05:04.255 --> 00:05:05.894
Excellent answer, Visal!

85
00:05:06.783 --> 00:05:11.502
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and it's important to plus verb.

86
00:05:11.802 --> 00:05:17.136
Today's value is self-discipline. Control your habits, so your habits do not control you.

87
00:05:17.436 --> 00:05:20.042
See you in Unit eighteen. Goodbye!

88
00:05:20.342 --> 00:05:22.879
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

